5543711483479, 0.0019094354938715696], "index": 7, "object": "embedding"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7037, "total_tokens": 7037}}, "input": {"input": ["Action: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-17\nValid as Of: 2024-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2096 ---\nComponent: Java Server\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Tomcat version for Java Web Tomcat 9 and Java EE 7 Web Profile TomEE 7\nDescription: Java Web Tomcat 9 (runtime version 4.88) and Java EE 7 Web Profile TomEE 7 (runtime version 1.186) have been updated to Tomcat version 9.0.95.  See the Changelog.  Recommended action: Update your applications to the latest runtime version.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-17\nValid as Of: 2024-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2097 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Connectivity Proxy for Kubernetes - New Features\nDescription: Connectivity Proxy version 2.13.0 provides the following new features:    The Connectivity Proxy now exposes various JVM and component-specific Prometheus metrics.  [Helm] You can now configure the topology key for the pod anti-affinity of each pod related to the Connectivity Proxy. This gives you more control over pod scheduling.  [Helm] You can now configure the request and limit resource constraints for the Region Configuration Controller micro-service of the Connectivity Proxy.  Support for custom PKI (public key infrastructure): The Connectivity Proxy now provides a list of certificate authorities which it should trust in addition to the default ones when performing outbound HTTPS calls is now supported.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-17\nValid as Of: 2024-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2098 ---\nComponent: Connectivity\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Connectivity Proxy for Kubernetes - Security Fixes\nDescription: Connectivity Proxy version 2.13.0 provides the following security fixes:      Multiple OS vulnerabilities by removing or upgrading packages on the image were fixed.      Multiple Java vulnerabilities by upgrading dependencies to a newer version were fixed.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-17\nValid as Of: 2024-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2099 ---\nComponent: Credential Store\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: CMK Encryption Details\nDescription: You can now easily set alert notifications on service instance level from the SAP Credential Store user interface, tab Settings. See:       Multiple Expiring Credential Bindings      Maximum Number of Credential Bindings      Maximum Number of Credentials      Maximum Number of Requests      Maximum Used Storage (in MB)    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-08\nValid as Of: 2024-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2100 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription:   Improvements were made to support validation of rural addresses in Chechia that consist of a house number on an unnamed road.   The microservice now returns the two numbers in street addresses in Chechia and Slovakia in the following output field properties. It returns the first number (registration number) in std_addr_building_name, the second number (orientation number) in std_addr_prim_number, and both numbers separated by a slash in std_addr_prim_number_full. See House Number for more information.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-10-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2261 ---\nComponent: Object Store\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Continuous backup on AWS\nDescription: Object Store now supports continuous backup and point-in time restoration on AWS. See Enable Continuous Backup and Request Point-in-Time Restoration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-19\nValid as Of: 2024-09-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2262 ---\nComponent: Object Store\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Role-based service bindings on Google Cloud Platform\nDescription: Object Store now supports read and write role-based service binding credentials. See Role-Based Bindings and Service Keys (Google Cloud).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-19\nValid as Of: 2024-09-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2263 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New SAP Alert Notification service event\nDescription: You can now use the newly supported SAP Alert Notification service event - Delivery Status.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-19\nValid as Of: 2024-09-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2264 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: New SAP Alert Notification service event\nDescription: You can now use the newly supported SAP Alert Notification service event - Delivery Status.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-19\nValid as Of: 2024-09-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2265 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New SAP Automation Pilot events\nDescription: You can now use the newly supported SAP Automation Pilot events - Command Created, Command Deleted, Command Updated, Input Created, Input Deleted and Input Updated\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-19\nValid as Of: 2024-09-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2266 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 42.2.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 42.1.0 to 42.2.0.    https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v42.2.0  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-19\nValid as Of: 2024-09-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2267 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Read-only in Form Tables\nDescription: Previously, you can only set the complete table to read only. Now you can select single columns and mark them as read only. However, this feature only protects against accidental overwriting of content. Users can still tweak their browsers to change the content.  For more information, see Form Tables.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-19\nValid as Of: 2024-09-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2268 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Transporting a Local App with a Card Visualization\nDescription: It is now possible to transport a local app with a card visualization between landscapes.  Note  This is not relevant to standalone cards.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-19\nValid as Of: 2024-09-19\nVersion: 2409A\n\n--- Record 2269 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Sorting Local Pages\nDescription: Sorting local pages created in the Content Manager are sorted by ID.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology